From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:31:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cabinet: XPRESS compression, FDITruncateCabinet (3306)

COMPRESS_ALGORITHM_XPRESS was refused (ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED). The
Compression API now handles it, buffer mode and raw: the "plain LZ77" of
[MS-XCA] with a window of 8 KiB, flag words and 4-bit/byte/16-bit/32-bit
length fields (a chunk that does not get smaller is stored). The streams
match the examples of the specification byte for byte. XPRESS_HUFF and
LZMS are still refused.

FDITruncateCabinet was a stub returning ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED. It now
removes the folders from the given one on: their files, their data, the
link to a next cabinet (the last folder is gone) and the folder and file
tables are rewritten, the data of the folders that stay moves up, the size
field is updated and the file is truncated through the write function
with zero bytes, as documented. A folder number past the last changes
nothing.

Test: test/fastcab-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_XP_*, SG_MUTANT_TRUNC_*).

diff --git a/dlls/cabinet/compressapi.c b/dlls/cabinet/compressapi.c
index a7685f8..9ac5e87 100644
--- a/dlls/cabinet/compressapi.c
+++ b/dlls/cabinet/compressapi.c
